<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Toribio Montes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1749">1749</a>–<a href="/years/1830">1830</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Toribio Montes was a Spanish general sent by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> to put down the autonomous government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quito">Quito</a>. His forces took Quito in November 1812 and destroyed the last patriot army at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibarra">Ibarra</a> in December. As president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/real-audiencia-of-quito">Real Audiencia of Quito</a> until 1817 he followed a relatively conciliatory policy towards the defeated patriots.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/toribio-montes.jpg" alt="Toribio Montes" width="320" height="439" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Toribio_Montes_y_P%C3%A9rez.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
